# Loot bag instead of monster bodies (O435, owner 2026-11-08: "remover os corpos de criaturas mortos do jogo e deixar so
# aquela bagzinha"; server/README.md "Loot bag instead of corpses"). A killed monster that has a corpse leaves the item
# Game.setMonsterLootBag(bagId, keepIds) names (item 6068, the container the import fallback already used), whatever its
# own corpse attribute or Lua corpse field says. One hook: Monster::getLookCorpse, which Creature::getCorpse reads when a
# creature dies, so loot, the corpse owner, decay, the onDeath / onDropLoot events and every script that reads the corpse
# see an ordinary corpse container (the bag) and nothing else changes.
#   * a monster whose own corpse is 0 leaves nothing, as before;
#   * a monster whose own corpse id is in keepIds keeps it (the quest and boss corpses scripts look for by id);
#   * bagId 0, or never calling the function, is the old behaviour: the switch is `enabled` in
#     data/scripts/chaos/corpse_config.lua, applied by data/scripts/chaos/corpse_bag.lua at load and on every reload;
#   * players are never touched: Player::getLookCorpse is not changed and ChaosLootBag::corpseOf is only called from
#     Monster::getLookCorpse (guard: tools/patch_monster_corpses_test.py).
# New header src/chaoslootbag.h (pure function, tests in server/tools/chaoslootbag_test.cpp, CI).
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0088: patch -p1 < 0089-monster-loot-bag.patch, then rebuild (not compiled
# here: the base tree is not in git; the header is built and tested in CI, the three hunks dry-run checked on the base
# tree up to patch 0044).
